# Implementation Plan: Support Modulo Operator

## Overview

This plan details the modifications required to add modulo operator (`%`) support to the existing calculator CLI application. The calculator currently supports four arithmetic operations (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`) and needs to be extended to include the modulo operator.

## Current State

### Files to Modify

1. **`src/cli.ts`** - Core calculation logic and type definitions
2. **`src/index.ts`** - CLI command definitions using yargs
3. **`tests/unit.test.ts`** - Unit tests for the calculate function
4. **`tests/e2e.test.ts`** - End-to-end CLI tests

### Current Implementation

**`src/cli.ts` (lines 3-16):**
```typescript
export type Operator = "+" | "-" | "*" | "/";

export function calculate(left: number, operator: Operator, right: number): number {
  switch (operator) {
    case "+":
      return left + right;
    case "-":
      return left - right;
    case "*":
      return left * right;
    case "/":
      return left / right;
  }
}
```

**`src/index.ts` (lines 23-35):**
```typescript
.positional("operator", {
  type: "string",
  choices: ["+", "-", "*", "/"] as const,
  demandOption: true,
})
// ...
const operator = argv.operator as "+" | "-" | "*" | "/";
```

